# A piece of a text that is only parsed, converted, compared with a written text or appended is never made: the operation reads the code units [start, end) out of the text itself.
# The two ends come out of a clamp against the length, which leaves its lower half out where the walk has told that the position is no less than nought, or straight from the walk.
# Under TestsEveryPosition and under CheckProofsAtRunTime each reader asks `start <= end <= length` where it stands (BelowEqual, twice) and stops by name.
# f1 = parsed, f2 = converted, f3 = compared, f4 = joined. The append asks BelowEqual for the room of its builder in every build, four times in this function: there the two more are the witness.
# RUN(PARSED): emit f1:Body mechanisms=all
# PARSED-NOT: BelowEqual
# RUN(PARSEDHELD): emit f1:Body mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition
# PARSEDHELD: BelowEqual
# RUN(CONVERTED): emit f2:Body mechanisms=all
# CONVERTED-NOT: BelowEqual
# RUN(CONVERTEDHELD): emit f2:Body mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition
# CONVERTEDHELD: BelowEqual
# RUN(COMPARED): emit f3:Body mechanisms=all
# COMPARED-NOT: BelowEqual
# RUN(COMPAREDHELD): emit f3:Body mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition
# COMPAREDHELD: BelowEqual
# RUN(JOINED): emit f4:Body mechanisms=all
# JOINED-COUNT-4: BelowEqual
# JOINED-NOT: BelowEqual
# RUN(JOINEDHELD): emit f4:Body mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition
# JOINEDHELD-COUNT-6: BelowEqual
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition
# ANSWERS: 16740 123,234,345,456,567,678,789,
